KZ2 patch 6065: GCM_FAST_METHODS, method-loop fast path under live draw. Default off.

From Killzone 3 port patch 2149 (KZ3 an earlier change; the Killzone 3 PC port "Project Helghast", same author, MIT; read at Project Helghast
port/patches/2149-gcm-fast-methods-under-live-draw.patch, snapshot work/kz3-import/2026-11-04-walker). Default off, as in KZ3.

gcm_word_diag() is split into gcm_word_diag_only() (the GCM_* diagnostic switches, which keep the per-word path) and
gcm_word_live() (live draw / draw engine). Before, any live consumer forced the per-word loop with a gcm_io2ea() translation
and a dozen checks per data word, so the contiguous-page run path never ran under live draw. With GCM_FAST_METHODS=1 and
no diagnostic switch, a method header on subchannel 0 or 1 with method != 0 whose data words lie in one 1 MB IO page
translates once and loops over the words: live feed, draw engine, driver methods (0xEB00/0xEB04, 0xE920/0xE924), then
the 3D or 2D dispatch exactly as the per-word loop routes it (gcm_subch1_nv0039 per word), in the per-word loop's order.
KZ2 changes against 2149: KZ2 has no RSX_PERF_X sampling and no gcm_subch1_nv0039_run, so the subchannel-1 routing is
decided per word as in the loop; KZ2's per-word KZ2_TGT_LOG note (patch 6011) turns the fast path off while it is set.
Host test tools/runtime/test_walker73.sh (synthetic ring, increment and non-increment headers, subchannel 1, a page
edge: identical call streams with the switch off and on).

